        "Initial omnific models of discrete initial surreal groups \u2014 Alec Kriebel, v1.0.0 (2026-10-17). Problem30003321, Kaplan with Ehrlich, OWR60/2016 suppliedprinted3356 Question1; earlier Kaplan2015thesisQ1p47 and sequel authorQ9.1p15. Full affirmative additive-group solution: every discrete initial subgroup G of No is order-group-isomorphic ONTO H contained in Oz initial in No, for sets/proper classes in NBG+global choice, zero separately. No multiplication or original-simplicity-preservation requirement. Explicit ordinal sign rerooting reflects target right prefixes; actual source supports and bottom-only coefficient scaling give the initial image. Seven-page note includes a detailed characterization sufficiency proof repairing cofinal-support exhaustion and legal-cut-option details, with direct Z-adjunction and class-to-set restrictions. Main construction unchanged. Earlier EK least-positive/characterization, ADH negative-ordinal minimum and generic exponent/coefficient transport credited. Bounded primary priority found no earlier recorded full target in inspected material; unread2024chapter/full2001/Lurie1998/other access gaps disclosed, no novelty/firstness/current-global-openness certificate. Extensive AI assistance; unrefereed, no external human peer review or formal certification. Two successive fresh no-history complete-package reviews passed the identical release. Two complete finite-sign positive outputs normal/optimized,8actual computed-property failures; finite diagnostics supplement universal proof. https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1151 Published record: https://zenodo.org/records/23444606"
